OL,3,GNEWSAWhat do we still need to know
OL,4,Aabout the Tyne nurdle spill?
OL,5,
OL,6,FOn 19 July about 18 tonnes of plastic
OL,7,Fnurdles, consisting of hundreds of
OL,8,Fmillions of tiny balls, spilled into
OL,9,Fthe River Tyne after a crash between
OL,10,Fships at the Port of Tyne.
OL,12,FIt is believed to be the worst recorded
OL,13,Fincident of its type in Europe.
OL,15,FIn the months since, teams of
OL,16,Fvolunteers have joined in efforts to
OL,17,Fcollect the microplastics that continue
OL,18,Fto wash up on north-east England's
OL,19,Fcoast.
OL,23,APub: 26-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
